{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /workspace && ls -la packet/ && echo \"=== incident_packet.md ===\" && cat packet/incident_packet.md && echo \"=== findings.json ===\" && cat packet/findings.json'","aggregated_output":"total 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 1000 1000 4096 May 14 04:43 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 1000 1000 4096 May 14 04:44 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1000 1000 1149 May 14 04:44 findings.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 1000 1000  893 May 14 04:43 incident_packet.md\n=== incident_packet.md ===\n# Incident Packet: INC-2047\n\n## Triggering Condition\nBulk refund requests were accepted without idempotency keys when the `legacy_batch_header` was present, allowing duplicate refunds to be processed.\n\n## Failed Guardrail\nThe idempotency-required guardrail was bypassed at 10:18 UTC due to the `legacy_batch_header` flag being honored. This allowed non-idempotent bulk refund operations to proceed.\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-Up Action\nReject all bulk-refund requests that do not include an idempotency key. Remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the bulk-refund endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\nThe initial theory (TICKET-8721) that a queue worker replayed an old payment event was opened before API gateway logs were available. This theory remains unverified, though TICKET-8729 provides stronger evidence pointing to the missing idempotency keys as the root cause.\n=== findings.json ===\n{\n  \"ranked_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"bulk-refund requests accepted without idempotency keys\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"timeline/incident_timeline.md: bulk refund requests accepted without idempotency keys at 10:17 UTC\", \"tickets/TICKET-8729.md: every duplicate has request_class=bulk-refund and no idempotency key\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"idempotency-required guardrail skipped for legacy_batch_header\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"timeline/incident_timeline.md: idempotency-required guardrail skipped due to legacy_batch_header at 10:18 UTC\", \"remediation/notes.md: remove the legacy_batch_header bypass before re-enabling the endpoint\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"reject bulk-refund requests without idempotency keys and remove legacy_batch_header bypass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\"remediation/notes.md: bulk-refund requests must be rejected unless they include an idempotency key\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_ambiguity\": \"worker replay was an early symptom theory (TICKET-8721) but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence in TICKET-8729\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
